<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Wuling of Zhao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 295 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Wuling of Zhao ruled the state of Zhao in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 325 to 299 BCE. In 307 BCE he ordered his army to adopt the trousers and mounted archery of the steppe nomads, a reform that made Zhao a leading military power, and he conquered the state of Zhongshan, whose annexation was completed in 296 BCE. After abdicating he was starved to death in a succession struggle in 295 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-wuling-of-zhao.jpg" alt="King Wuling of Zhao" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (I am a wild crane.) 我乃野云鹤 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_King_Zhao_Wuling_in_Congtai_Park.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
